  "version": "2.6.0",
  "notes": "- On Windows, choose the installer or extract the portable ZIP and run `atv-optimizer.exe`. The ZIP comes with a SHA-256 checksum and requires Microsoft Edge WebView2. Settings and pairing keys stay in your Windows profile.\n- Android TV Optimizer is now the name on the installer and throughout the desktop app. It supports Android TV and Google TV, including NVIDIA Shield. The README shows supported workflows with demo screenshots.\n- Refresh RAM on demand, stop a measurement, and compare three launch trials before and after restricting background activity. Undo restores the saved restriction.\n- Browse installed apps in one table, manage APK versions, and find display, audio and input controls under device settings. The release also includes recording, mirroring, storage inspection and an activity console.\n- Updated to upstream `d62f4a4d` with device-specific support tiers, snapshot safeguards, and read-back checks for device settings. Existing fork installs keep their updater channel. Development copies already at 2.6.1 will skip this release.\n\n### First-run warnings\n\nThese builds are unsigned. Your OS may complain on first launch:\n\n- **macOS** (Gatekeeper): the first-launch dialog on macOS 15+ only offers \"Move to Trash\" or \"Done\" — click **Done**, then either:\n    - **Terminal:** `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine \"/Applications/Android TV Optimizer.app\"` (one-time, then double-click as normal)\n    - **GUI:** System Settings → Privacy & Security → scroll to the \"Android TV Optimizer was blocked\" message → **Open Anyway** → enter password\n- **macOS** (Local Network): click **Allow** when macOS asks to find devices on your local network. If no TV is found, click **Restart ADB**. If that doesn't help, open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Local Network, turn Android TV Optimizer off and on again (every entry, if it's listed more than once), then click **Restart ADB** again.\n- **Windows** (SmartScreen): \"More info\" → \"Run anyway\".\n- **Linux**: `chmod +x Android.TV.Optimizer*.AppImage` before running. For the Flatpak: `flatpak install --user Android.TV.Optimizer_*_x86_64.flatpak` (it doesn't update itself: install the next release's bundle the same way).\n\nSee the [README](https://github.com/LosLonelyDevs/AndroidTV-Optimizer#readme) for setup and feature docs.",
